    {
      "filename": "Green Sand Beach (Papakolea Beach) (17905163884).jpg",
      "title": "File:Green Sand Beach (Papakolea Beach) (17905163884).jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/37/Green_Sand_Beach_%28Papakolea_Beach%29_%2817905163884%29.jpg",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Green_Sand_Beach_(Papakolea_Beach)_(17905163884).jpg",
      "width": 4752,
      "height": 3168,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY 2.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0",
      "artist": "Pushkr from  , United States",
      "description": "This is one of very few green sand beaches in the world. Ride to this beach is quite an adventure. There is no easy way to go here unless you have UTV or high-powered all wheel drive. We hitched a ride with a local gentleman named John for $15 round trip pp. There is no proper road to reach here, its all just roughest terrain with mud puddles, rocks and whatnot. We saw so many 'all terrain' SUVs stuck on the way here. \n\n\nDont even think about driving your rental car here.",
      "dateCreated": "2015-03-05 19:08",
